Subject: [PATCH] drm: bridge: lt9611: retain ring clock for DT510 diagnosis

Temporary A/B test, NOT a product clock configuration. Build 692 confirms
that selecting the crystal at 0x8101=0x18 precedes the first STOP timeout
and unsuccessful bus clear. Keep the system-clock source on the reset
ring oscillator by writing 0x08, preserving the ring bias-current bits.
Change no other sequence, delay, retry, reset or controller setting.

Observe first-start I2C completion and EDID separately from display
timing. The frequency-meter constants assume the crystal reference;
ring-clock video/DDC timing is not qualified. A pass isolates dependence
on clock selection, not a defective crystal or a production-ready fix.
Remove this diagnostic patch after the controlled comparison.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [temporary DT510 clock-source diagnostic]
Assisted-by: Briar
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/lontium-lt9611.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/lontium-lt9611.c
@@ -489,7 +489,7 @@
 	int ret, attempt;
 	const struct reg_sequence seq[] = {
 		/* LT9611_System_Init */
-		{ 0x8101, 0x18 }, /* sel xtal clock */
+		{ 0x8101, 0x08 }, /* TEST ONLY: retain ring clock, not qualified timings */
 
 		/* timer for frequency meter */
 		{ 0x821b, 0x69 }, /* timer 2 */
